# Netlify redirect rules for the published site. Netlify reads this file from
# the publish root; the private repository's build.sh copies it into dist/.
#
# Short link for outreach: the standalone demo is the primary "Live Demo" target
# (see README.md), and <your-domain>/demo is what fits in an email. A 301 rather
# than a rewrite so the address bar ends on the canonical URL that the page's
# own <link rel="canonical"> already declares — a rewrite would serve the same
# content at two addresses and split the signal.
#
# The trailing `!` forces the rule: Netlify otherwise skips a redirect whose
# path resolves to an existing file, and `/demo` would resolve to demo.html
# if that page were ever published again. Forced, `/demo` is always the
# standalone demo — which is why its _headers rule can be the strict policy.
/demo    /demo-standalone.html    301!

# www -> apex is NOT set here on purpose. Netlify does that itself once a
# primary domain is chosen in Domain settings, and hardcoding one direction
# would fight that setting (and loop) if the other is picked.

# The assessor page was /3pao.html until the buyer-facing rename to
# "Independent Assessment Services". Anything already linking the old path —
# outreach emails, a partner's site, a search result — has to keep landing.
/3pao.html    /assessors.html    301

# The social card's SOURCE is not a page. It lives beside the PNG it renders
# (static/og-card.png) so the binary stays rebuildable, and check.mjs 22 holds
# it there — but publish = "." means everything in the tree is deployed, and it
# was reachable at these two addresses with no Content-Security-Policy, because
# _headers declares a policy per page and this is not one. A wildcard CSP is not
# the fix (see the note at the top of _headers: Netlify combines matching rules
# and a browser intersects them, so /* could only silently tighten each page's
# own). Making the addresses 404 is.
#
# Forced, for the reason the /demo rule above documents: Netlify skips a
# redirect whose path resolves to an existing file, and this file exists.
/static/og-card.src.html    /404.html    404!
/static/og-card.src         /404.html    404!
